      "message": "Looks okay.  As I mentioned in chat, this bug might exist on older kernels too; it might have gotten exposed by some userspace program trying to read past EOF.  So please make sure to fix incfs in older kernels as needed.\n\nIt is a bit odd to be using PageChecked as both the checked flag and the \"real\" up-to-date flag.  I think it works, but it would be more self-explanatory if PageUptodate was used for the contents of the page while PageChecked was used for whether the page has been checked.  This would require that incfs\u0027s -\u003ereadpage() method be updated to actually fill (but not necessarily check) Merkle tree pages, rather than fill them with all zeroes.  This would match what ext4 and f2fs do.",
